<title>UK: British Fittings H1 pretax profit edges up.</title>
<headline>British Fittings H1 pretax profit edges up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		2.11		   vs 2.85</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 1.35		   vs 1.20</p>
<p> Pretax		     1.32		   vs 1.26</p>
<p> Turnover		   39.10		  vs 38.86</p>
<p> Operating result	 2.36		   vs 1.89</p>
<p> Interest		   0.46		   vs 0.62</p>
<p> Tax			  0.62		   vs 0.39</p>
<p> Retained profit	  0.18		   vs 0.39</p>
<p> Pay date		   November 22</p>
<p>Div registration date  October 22 Note - Earnings per share excluding disposal of subsidiaries were 4.19 pence in the six months ending June 30.</p>
<p>It took an exceptional charge of 495,000 stg for loss on the sale of a subsidiary.</p>
<p>British Fittings Group Plc is an industrial manufacturer and distributor.</p>
<p>Chairman Michael Borlenghi said in a statement that the second half had started ahead of last year, but demand generally continues to be sluggish. &quot;We remain optimistic about the medium-term future,&quot;  he said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
